00:14:27,190 --> 00:16:03,550
Rep. Jose Manuel “Chel” I. Diokno: Thank you. If Your Honor is pleased, good morning. Good morning to our colleagues in the defense panel. For context, Your Honor, the prosecution filed a request for admission. to narrow the matters genuine in dispute, conserve the Honorable Court's valuable time for issues that truly require evidence and resolution, and ensure that the proceedings are conducted fairly and efficiently for the benefit of all the parties. Inihain po namin ang request for admission upang maging mas maayos at mabilis ang paglilitis po nitong kaso. Ito lang po ang aming layunin na tukuyin kung alin ang tunay na pinagtatalunan nang hindi na kailangan ubusin Ang oras ng hukuman sa mga bagay na maaari namang kilalanin o hindi naman talaga kontrobersyal. The request covers certain self-evident and factual matters, including records produced and submitted directly by several banks in compliance with the subpoenas issued by this court. Among others, the respondent was simply requested to admit or deny the existence, genuineness, and authenticity of these bank records. On September 23, 2026, the respondent filed her objection. She principally argues that Rule 26 is supposedly inapplicable to impeachment proceedings, that requiring her to answer would supposedly violate her right against self-incrimination and improperly shift the burden of proof, and that certain requested matters allegedly implicate marital or filial privileges are irrelevant or fall outside

